From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:11:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: leds: pwm: Add an optional duty cycle
 range

Some PWM LEDs must not run at full duty, and some stay dark below a
threshold duty cycle. Add min-duty-cycle-bp and max-duty-cycle-bp, in
basis points of the period: brightness b > 0 gives
min + (max - min) * b / max-brightness, and brightness 0 is off.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
(cherry picked from commit b2f70f243d12c7ede7d6837268294a15623f21b1)
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/leds/leds-pwm.yaml    | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/leds-pwm.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/leds-pwm.yaml
index 6c4fcefbe2..8d81e428fa 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/leds-pwm.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/leds/leds-pwm.yaml
@@ -34,6 +34,26 @@ patternProperties:
           Maximum brightness possible for the LED
         $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
 
+      min-duty-cycle-bp:
+        description:
+          Start of the PWM duty cycle range, in basis points (1/100 of a
+          percent) of the period. Brightness b from 1 to max-brightness gives
+          min-duty-cycle-bp + (max-duty-cycle-bp - min-duty-cycle-bp) * b /
+          max-brightness; brightness 0 is off. Use it for an LED that stays
+          dark below a threshold duty cycle.
+        minimum: 0
+        maximum: 9999
+        default: 0
+
+      max-duty-cycle-bp:
+        description:
+          PWM duty cycle at max-brightness, in basis points of the period.
+          Use it for an LED that must not be driven above a fraction of full
+          duty.
+        minimum: 1
+        maximum: 10000
+        default: 10000
+
       default-brightness:
         description:
           Brightness to be set if LED's default state is on. Used only during
